==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|ang|en}} {{term/t|ang|eorþlīċ}}, corresponding to {{suffix|earth|ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈəːθli/}}
* {{audio|en-us-earthly.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Relating to the [[earth]] or this world, as opposed to heaven.
#: '''''earthly''' joys''
#* Milton
#*: This '''earthly''' load / Of death, called life.
#* Bible, Phil. iii. 19
#*: whose glory is in their shame, who mind '''earthly''' things
# {{context|negative|informal|lang=en}} {{non-gloss definition|Used to put an emphasis}}
#* Alexander Pope
#*: What '''earthly''' benefit can be the result?
# Made of earth; [[earthy]].
#: {{rfquotek|Holland}}

====Translations====
{{trans-top|as opposed to heaven}}
* Bulgarian: [[земен, светски]]
* Russian: {{t+|ru|земной|tr=zemnój|sc=Cyrl}}, {{t+|ru|мирской|tr=mirskój|sc=Cyrl}}, {{t+|ru|суетный|tr=sújetnyj|sc=Cyrl}}, {{t+|ru|светский|tr=svétskij|sc=Cyrl}}
{{trans-mid}}
{{trans-bottom}}

